course: dictionary
lesson: 1244
title: Words that travelled
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some English words came from other languages a long time ago. You can use the words around a new word to find its meaning. «Priya's grandma in Leicester smiles: "Pyjamas, shampoo and bungalow are Hindi words, beta!"» Beta is a loving word for a child, so grandma is talking to Priya kindly.
explain: Now read the word bungalow in context. A bungalow is a house with only one floor, so there are no stairs to an upstairs. People talk about «a seaside bungalow» or «live in a bungalow», so it is a kind of home.
explain: Meanings can change from place to place. In older Indian use, a bungalow was a large one-storey house with a veranda. In the United States, it can mean a small, cosy house with a low roof and a porch. A dictionary helps you check which meaning fits your sentence.
fact: A bungalow is a house with only one floor.
fact: Bungalows have no stairs to an upstairs, so they are easy to move around in.
fact: «Pyjamas», «shampoo» and «bungalow» came from Hindi and Urdu during British rule in India.
fact: «Beta» is a loving word for a child in Hindi and Urdu.
fact: In the United States, a bungalow can be a small, cosy house with a low roof and a porch.
exercise: What is a bungalow? | A tall house with five floors and a lift | A shop that sells bread | A boat that floats on a lake | *A house with only one floor and no stairs to an upstairs
exercise: Grandma says pyjamas, shampoo and bungalow are Hindi words. What does this tell us? | They are all names of animals | They were invented in London last year | They are all names of food | *They came from Hindi and Urdu during British rule in India
exercise: Which word in «Pyjamas, shampoo and bungalow are Hindi words» is the name of a home? | Shampoo | *Bungalow | Hindi | Pyjamas
test: In the United States, a bungalow can mean what? | A large ship that sails across the sea | *A small, cosy house with a low roof and a porch | A garden shed for tools | A school for young children
test: Why might an older person like to live in a bungalow? | *Because there are no stairs to climb | Because it floats on water | Because it is always underground | Because it has ten bedrooms and a swimming pool
exam: What does «beta» mean in Priya's grandma's sentence? | The name of a city in India | *A loving word for a child | A type of pyjamas | A kind of shampoo
